{
  "description": "Integer boundaries. Internal counters are ordinary JSON integers with Rust range checks: a 64-bit sequence or revision at its maximum is valid, deadline_ms must be 1..=60000, and a negative or out-of-range value is a rejection on both ends (a negative integer cannot even decode into the unsigned Rust field: wrong_type). Ruby validates deadline_ms the same way; it never emits negative counters.",
